A||||4||Jncomutt||I have no lights, just headlights||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||08-18-2001||11:47 PM||||I left my car opened and unattended at work today (something I never do)  When I heard a co-worker was sitting in it, (he asks 100 times to but never let him)I went to check it out and the headlights were up.  But no lights on... I checked the switch, it was down...  I thought it could have been a fuse or sumthin, didn't think much of it...  But as I was driving home tonight,  I had no dash lights either.  Also, none of the marker lights or rear lights were on either.  They come on if you hit the brakes, but other than that, nothing.<P>I checked all the fuses, they were all OK.  I did a search and found that it could be a relay, or the headlight switch...  I'm not really sure what a relay even is or how to check a relay.  Also is it anything else there could be??<P>I heard the reason they wouldn't go down could be related to the taillaps.  Last week I created my own clear taillights (I put two of the clear center pieces in, and then 3 blocks of the red for the curved part of the corner) and installed red bulbs.  They were the right part #, I picked em up at pep boys and have had em in for about 9 days, no prob.  Could it be because the bulbs toasted a relay??  Or my switch could be bad because I did armor-all my interior earlier in the day, would that matter???  Any info is appreciated, As always...<P>EDIT:  Oh yea, if I crank my headlights down, they will come up when you press the switch.  And if you push just the parking light part of the switch, nothing happens, I don't even get the "reminder chime"<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-19-2001||12:35 AM||||It sure sounds like your taillight fuse is blown.  Please check it again.<P>Is it possible your custom taillights draw too much current (significantly more amps than the original equipment setup)?  Or, might you have accidentally created a short circuit while you were working on the taillights/side markers?<P>Is it possible I ask too many questions  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?  Good luck, and good night  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||10:11 AM||||tail, marker, park and panel lites are all on same fuse. I dont think theres any relays on them. If its not the fuse make the guy pay to fix what he screwed up. He prob was flipping everything. I never mess with other peoples cars and hate it when people gotta touch. flipping switch could have gotten some armorall in it. HOW MANY TIMES I GOTTA TELL YOU GUYS TO THROW THAT CRAP AWAY !!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">it serves no worthwile purpose except to make junk used cars look pretty for dealers to sell to you.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||08-19-2001||12:01 PM||||Woo Hoo.. fixed it, sort of.  I double checked the fuses, and once again, you guys were right.  I had a 10amp instead of a 20.  The fuse was still good however...  I tested it.  I replaced it with the 20 and the headlights went right down.  The problem I have now is that the driver side tailights don't come on with the parking lights.  They come on with the brakes, the blinker, or hazard, but still no parking.  If I shake the wires, the on I am shaking comes on.  when I let go, it will go off.  I decided to put the red bulbs back in, and everything was fine, everything worked.  Could they have stretched the lightbulb housing so they regular bulbs don't catch?  Or do you think theres a short and just leaving the red bulbs won't fix it...||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||03:17 PM||||leave the switch off take out all the bulbs that are having trouble. clean out any goop in the sockets with something like a toothpick and spray inside them good with some electrical contact cleaner. then blow it all dry. youll be able to see if any contacts are bent or broke. put the bulbs back in and see if they work. If still have probs make sure the bulbs you have ARE good. if still dont work, you got some broken wire inside their insulation or a bad ground somewhere.||||reg||1
